Now an important Google follow-up

The interviewer may ask:

"Why do we use index instead of a used[] array for Subsets?"

Think about what happens with:

[1,2,3]

For subsets, once we've made the decision about 1, we never need to go backwards 
and reconsider it at a different position.

We're always moving:

index → index + 1

So index itself tells us which elements are still available for consideration.

used[] is unnecessary.

That is different from permutations, where an element can be selected at any remaining position, 
so we need explicit tracking of which elements are already used.


🔥 This gives you a powerful comparison
Subsets
       State = index + path
       Choice = include / exclude

Permutations
         State = path + used
         Choice = choose any unused element

This distinction is much more important than memorizing either code template.
